      "id": "claim_babe4b2f68f74f2e9a7ffcdc8135f6c5",
      "statement": "chat uses a persistent SQLite checkpoint file (~/.openwiki/openwiki.sqlite) so a conversation resumes across turns, while init/update use an in-memory checkpointer; because a chat session reuses one thread_id and SqliteSaver never prunes, persistent chat history is trimmed to the latest checkpoint per thread after each turn. The repository page-job lifecycle uses no LangGraph checkpointer at all, relying on .run.json for durability.",
